WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.936
-I want to start off
by addressing

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.504
a couple rumors that I've heard.
-Uh-oh.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.339
-Okay? They're all good.
-All right.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.641
-First rumor -- you've been
working on new music.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.876
-This is true.
-Really?

00:00:10.876 --> 00:00:12.244
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:14.581
-'Cause I love your stuff.
-Thank you so much.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:16.749
Yes, I've been working --
I've been working

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:18.518
on a lot of music
for a long time,

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:19.919
and my fans
are very aware of that.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.954
And they've been so patient,
which I'm so thankful for

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:23.856
because I've had some really
wonderful opportunities

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:26.626
that have kind of taken me away
from the music

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:27.894
for periods of time.

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:30.796
But I can say
that early next year,

00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:32.065
new music will be out.

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:33.533
-Early next year.
All right. Good.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.168
Good, good, good. I love that.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:37.603
Second rumor.
-Yes.

00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:40.372
-Is it true that you set up
Sophie Turner and Joe Jonas?

00:00:40.372 --> 00:00:41.907
-No. Are they saying that?

00:00:41.907 --> 00:00:43.743
I will totally take credit
for that if they're saying it.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.110
-Yeah. No, that's what I heard.
-Really?

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:46.712
-I heard you set them up.

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:48.914
-I definitely got the, like,
"Tell me about Joe Jonas" call.

00:00:48.914 --> 00:00:50.783
-Oh, really?
-Sophie and I -- Yeah.

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:52.886
Sophie and I have been friends
for years.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.255
She's one of my favorite humans.
And Joe, same.

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.256
Joe and I worked together
a couple years ago,

00:00:57.256 --> 00:00:59.525
and he is also
a wonderful person.

00:00:59.525 --> 00:01:01.527
-Yeah.
-And it worked, so...

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:03.195
Yeah, I'll take credit for that.
Sure.

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:05.198
-Yeah -- Yeah. So she just
called you up and said,

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:06.866
"Hey, I'm dating Joe Jonas."
-Well, no.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.068
She called me,
and she was like -- This is --

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:11.504
I don't remember when,
but she called and said --

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.772
Because she knew that I knew him

00:01:13.772 --> 00:01:15.841
and sort of asked
for my opinion.

00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:17.510
-Yeah.
-I gave her the truth.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.112
I won't tell -- I won't say
everything I said to her.

00:01:20.112 --> 00:01:21.547
-Yeah, yeah. All right. Good.

00:01:21.547 --> 00:01:24.050
-No, I gave her
my stamp of approval.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.985
-And now they're married.
-And now they're married.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.287
-Yeah, that's fantastic.
-Yeah.

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:28.721
-See? All right, good.
You helped her out.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:31.257
All right. Good.
Now let's talk "Dickinson."

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.992
-Yes.
-Emily Dickinson.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:37.897
This is on Apple TV+.
This is the debut of Apple TV+.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.832
-Yes, it is.
-November 1st.

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.333
-November 1st, this show --
-It's the whole thing.

00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:42.635
It's brand-new.
It's changing the game.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.136
-The whole thing is coming.
I know. I'm very excited.

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:47.140
It's been so wonderful to see
it all sort of come together,

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.874
and it's actually,
finally, happening.

00:01:48.874 --> 00:01:50.943
-How is it working with Apple?
Do you like that?

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:52.411
-Oh, yeah.
It's really incredible.

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:54.847
They are -- I mean, it's Apple.

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:56.983
-Yeah, I know.
They're pretty big.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.651
But can you -- Answer me this.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.887
Is it like Netflix
where, like --

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:03.289
Do you get all the episodes
at once?

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:07.193
-So, in our case, you will be
able to get all 10 episodes

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.729
of "Dickinson" on November 1st,
when the platform launches.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.197
Which is very exciting.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:15.901
And it's, in my opinion,
very easy to binge this show.

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.770
So I'm very excited about that.
-It's binge-worthy. Yes.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.206
-Very binge-worthy I think.
-And you were at the big event

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.442
they had like,
in Cupertino or whatever.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.010
-Yes. Yeah.
-With like --

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.979
It was you, it was,
uh, Jennifer Aniston.

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:27.347
-Jennifer Aniston.
-Oprah.

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:28.781
-Oprah was there.
-Come on.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.349
Look at the picture
of you and Oprah.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:32.184
-Photo evidence, people.

00:02:32.184 --> 00:02:34.720
-Photo or didn't happen.
Come on. How great?

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.890
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.724
I love -- I love Oprah.
She just --

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:41.260
-I mean, yeah. She --
It was the most insane thing.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.297
I had met her previously before

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:46.032
and, of course, saw her there.
-Yeah.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:49.669
-And debated, you know,
of course, saying hello.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:53.339
But then a million reasons not
to do that came into my brain.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.741
So I didn't.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:55.974
But then, before I knew it,

00:02:55.974 --> 00:02:57.943
Oprah sort of tapped me
on the shoulder and said,

00:02:57.943 --> 00:02:59.645
"Hailee, it's so great
to see you."

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:02.015
And I forgot every word
in the English language.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:04.117
I had no idea
what to do with my hands.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.818
I was just --
Then she asked for a photo.

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.553
And I don't think
I've ever looked happier

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:09.221
in a photo in my life.
-You really are.

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:11.157
Yeah, you were having
a great time there, yeah.

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:13.193
That's very good.
-Oh, God.

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:16.896
-Let's talk about
producing "Dickinson."

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.731
You're producing "Dickinson."
-Yes, I am.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:22.501
-Why? Why did you produce it?
-Well -- Yeah.

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.603
This is my first time
executive producing a project.

00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:26.239
-Do you like doing it?
-Yeah, I do.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:29.576
It's a -- It's a --
It's a different process.

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:31.811
-Yeah.
-But -- But really incredible

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:34.113
to be a part of something
that I do care so much about

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.682
and so moved by --

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:38.050
just being a part of, you know,

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:39.451
certain
decision-making processes

00:03:39.451 --> 00:03:41.120
and seeing something
really come together

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.188
from the beginning,
middle, to the end.

00:03:43.188 --> 00:03:46.058
-Were you a fan of
Emily Dickinson before this?

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:50.596
-I knew of her poetry, having
read some of it in high school,

00:03:50.596 --> 00:03:53.065
but I didn't know much
about her.

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:55.835
And I'm so thankful
for this show

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:58.070
and having had the opportunity
to play her,

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.939
because she truly is quite
an interesting human,

00:04:00.939 --> 00:04:02.674
and I think the world

00:04:02.674 --> 00:04:04.543
will agree, hopefully,
when they see the show.

00:04:04.543 --> 00:04:05.978
-It's good.
It's beautifully shot.

00:04:05.978 --> 00:04:07.714
And, also, some good laughs
in there, too.

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:09.515
-Yes.
-And Wiz Khalifa.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.218
-Wiz Khalifa's in the show.
-How -- How did that happen?

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:14.420
-That's a great question.
-Yeah.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.289
-Well, so, Emily has --

00:04:17.289 --> 00:04:21.094
You can pick this up
after reading one poem.

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:22.828
She's got the most wild
imagination.

00:04:22.828 --> 00:04:25.264
She has this sort of fascination
with death

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:26.933
and the idea of death.

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:30.069
And in our show, Wiz Khalifa
plays the character of Death,

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:32.538
who Emily is, again, fascinated

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:35.808
and sort of in love with,
in a sense.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:40.980
And so we wanted basically
the coolest person ever

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.614
to play this character and --

00:04:42.614 --> 00:04:44.716
-Yeah, and I wasn't available.
-With -- Well, right.

00:04:44.716 --> 00:04:46.585
-And so --
-Well, we went --

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:48.821
-Thank you, yeah.
-Yeah, no sure.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:51.891
But that was Wiz.
Second to you, so...

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.260
-And how was --
How was Wiz to work with?

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.695
-He was great.
-I love him.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:57.596
-He's wonderful.
Best sense of humor.

00:04:57.596 --> 00:04:59.098
Always -- Well, yeah.
He's always laughing,

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:02.635
but I mean, I guess,
we might know why?

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:04.370
-Yeah, usually when people
are around him,

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:05.972
everyone's laughing.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:07.573
-He's always having a good time.

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.208
-It's great.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:11.143
Here's Hailee Steinfeld
in "Dickinson."

00:05:11.143 --> 00:05:13.479
Take a look at this.

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.581
[ Knock on door ]

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.182
-Emily!

00:05:17.182 --> 00:05:19.018
[ Knock on door ]
Emily, wake up!

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:21.020
[ Knock on door ]
-Ugh!

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.457
-You have to go fetch water.

00:05:25.457 --> 00:05:28.394
-It is 4:00 in the morning,
Lavinia. I'm writing.

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:31.097
-Mother says you have to.
I did it yesterday.

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:34.834
-[ Sighs ]
Why doesn't Austin do it?

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.569
-Austin is a boy.

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:41.574
-This is such bull [bleep].

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:43.409
-Hailee Steinfeld, everybody.

